course: dictionary
lesson: 9120
title: Words that name places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A smokehouse is a place, and its name tells you what it is for: smoke plus house. You do not need a dictionary for every word. Read the words around it, and they will give you clues. «The hunter says the animals should show up in this dark place like ripe bananas in a smokehouse.» The sentence calls it a dark place, so a smokehouse is a room that is dark.
explain: The sentence also paints a picture: ripe bananas are bright yellow, so the animals will stand out like bright things in a dark room. The writer uses a comparison to help you see what is meant. When you meet a word for a place, ask what happens there and what it looks like.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try "a dark building where meat or fish is smoked" in place of "smokehouse". Does the sentence still make sense? If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: A smokehouse is a building or room where meat or fish is hung and smoked over a slow fire.
fact: Smoke was used to flavour food and to keep it from going bad.
fact: Before fridges, smoking and drying were ways to keep food fresh for longer.
fact: Today smokehouses make smoked salmon, kippers and bacon.
fact: In stories about farms and villages, a smokehouse is one of the outbuildings, the small buildings beside the main house.
exercise: «The hunter says the animals should show up in this dark place like ripe bananas in a smokehouse.» What is a smokehouse? | A place where people go to swim | A fruit shop with bananas for sale | A tall tower on a hill | *A building or room where meat or fish is hung and smoked over a slow fire
exercise: Why is meat hung in a smokehouse? | To make it cold and frozen | To turn it into a cake | *To flavour it and keep it from going bad | To wash it in clean water
exercise: Find and copy one word from the sentence that tells you the smokehouse is a dark place. | bananas | *dark | hunter | ripe
test: Before fridges, why did people smoke their food? | *To keep it from going bad | To paint it | To make it spicy | To make it bigger
test: Which of these is made in smokehouses today? | *Smoked salmon | Fresh bread | Orange juice | Ice cream
exam: In the sentence, what does «like ripe bananas» tell you about the animals? | Green and hard | Heavy to lift | *Bright and easy to see | Sweet and sticky
